# Gate of the ipu4p / ipu4p leg: the IPU4P baseline, Ruslan's tree
# (tools/ipu6/pin) without the IPU4 series, under the IPU4P QEMU model.
# Owned by the IPU4P variant track (tools/notes/ipu4p-variant-plan.md);
# each of its PRs enables one more test.
#
# One test name per line; '#' starts a comment. Every known test runs on
# every PR, but only the tests listed here fail the job; run
# `tools/tests/ipu6/ladder.sh --list` for the names.

# Static tests (P1). With no series, series-applies is the bare fetch and
# checkpatch has nothing to check.
series-applies
build
checkpatch

# Guest boot with the model presenting 8086:8a19 (ipu4p plan P2).
vm-boot

# virt-sensor + intel-ipu6* load/unload; intel-ipu6 probes 8a19 on load
# (ipu4p plan P2, which also covers P3).
module-load

# Probe identifies 8a19 as IPU4P (requests intel/ipu/ipu4p_fw.bin)
# (ipu4p plan P4).
probe-identify

# ISYS/PSYS power-up through IPU4P's PWR_STATE layout (ipu4p plan P5).
probe-buttress

# Forced ISYS runtime resume with ISYS bound (ipu4p plan P6).
isys-resume
